600 - Hold Fast Till I Come
 / 
Key: F
Time: 4/4
Tempo: Moderato
Number: 600
Topic: Christian Life - 

Verse 1:
[Bb]Sweet promise [C]is [C7]given to [F]all who believe—
[F]“Behold I come quickly, Mine own to receive;
[F]Hold fast till [Bb/F]Icome; [F]the danger is great;
[C]Sleep not [F/C]as do [C7]others; [F/C]be [C]watchful, [F]and wait.”

Refrain:
[F]"Hold fast [C]till I [C7]come," [F/C]sweet promise [C7]of heaven--
[F/A]"The kingdom restored, [C]to you shall [F]be given."
[F]"Come, enter [Bb/F]My joy, [F]sit down on the throne;
[C]Bright crowns [F/C]are in [C7]waiting; [F/C]hold [C7]fast [Gm/D]till I [Dm]come."

Verse 2:
[Bb]We'll "watch [C]unto [C7]prayer" with [F]lamps burning bright;
[F]He comes to all others a "thief in the night."
[F]We know He [Bb/F]is near, [F]but know not the day--
[C]As spring [F/C]shows that [C7]summer [F/C]is [C]not [F]far away.

Verse 3:
[Bb]Yes! this [C]is [C7]our hope, 'tis [F]built on His word--
[F]The glorious appearing of Jesus, our Lord;
[F]Of promises [Bb/F]all, [F]it stands as the sum:
[C]"Behold [F/C]I come [C7]quickly; [F/C]hold [C]fast [F]till I come."
